// THE ELITE DIARY REWARDS' EFFECTS (13 October, Corey: "do #10, #21, #15 ... for the diary items,
// those will all go in the vote shop - only the ones that are actually useful ... wire those up
// with their effects and add them to the vote shop; that is the only way to receive them", then
// "do only the level 4 items, not their lower tiers").
//
// WHY ONLY TIER 4. The twelve reward sets were imported whole (general/configs/diary_rewards.obj,
// four tiers each) but the achievement diary that hands them out does not exist in this build and
// is not what suggestion #15 asked for - the shop is. A shop selling four tiers of the same cape
// would be selling three strictly worse capes, so only the elite tier is for sale and the lower
// tiers stay what they have always been: unobtainable config.
//
// WHICH NINE. Of the twelve sets, nine are sold and wired:
//
//   Ardougne cloak 4        Monastery and Ardougne farm teleports
//   Desert amulet 4         Nardah and Kalphite cave teleports
//   Falador shield 4        two full Prayer recharges a day (scripts/falador_shield.rs2)
//   Fremennik sea boots 4   Rellekka teleport
//   Kandarin headgear 4     Seers' Village teleport
//   Karamja gloves 4        Shilo gem mine and Slayer master teleports
//   Morytania legs 4        Ectofuntus and Burgh de Rott teleports
//   Varrock armour 4        10% chance of a second ore (scripts/diary_passives.rs2)
//   Wilderness sword 4      Fountain of Rune teleport, and webs always cut
//
// THE THREE LEFT OUT, and why none of them is an oversight:
//
//   Western banner 4        Corey's call ("not the banner etc."). Its teleport is Gnome Stronghold,
//                           which the spirit tree and the gnome glider already reach.
//   Rada's blessing 4       both its teleports are Great Kourend, which this build has no map for.
//   Explorer's ring 4       already sold, already wired - it carries the farm teleport
//                           (skill_farming/scripts/farm_teleport.rs2) and was the shop's first row.
//
// WHAT IS NOT WIRED, said plainly rather than left to be discovered: the secondary passives that
// Old School attaches to an elite diary rather than to the item - Varrock armour's double smelt at
// the Edgeville furnace, the Kandarin flax-for-bowstring trade, Falador shield 1-3's Giant Mole
// pointer, the prospector-jacket experience bonus. Each of those lives in a skill or an NPC this
// file does not own, and the item's headline effect is what makes it worth buying.

// ============================================================================ the teleports
//
// COMPILE-TIME COORDS, not an enum. farm_teleport.rs2 needs an int -> coord enum because its
// destination is whatever the player picked out of a menu; here every option has exactly one
// destination, so the coord can be the literal the trigger passes in and there is no id space,
// no table, and no default to get wrong.
//
// SIX OF THESE ARE COREY'S OWN (13 October), and they replace six that were picked by measurement
// alone. The measurement answered "can a player stand here, and is it near the landmark" and got
// both right every time - and still landed in the wrong place twice, because near a landmark is
// not the same as where a player wants to be put down. The gem mine arrival was underground by
// the Karamja rocks when the mining site the teleport is for is on the surface outside Shilo; the
// Slayer master's was out on the landing rather than in the room with Duradel. The named coords
// win over the measured ones.
//
// EVERY ONE IS STILL CHECKED, which is the part the measurement keeps: engine/tools/sim/
// diaryrewards.ts asserts each is a tile the collision map says a player can stand on, that the
// landing matches the figure below, and that the walkable area it joins is the size recorded there
// - so a map import that walls one off fails the sim rather than landing somebody in a hedge.
//
// TWO ARE SMALL ON PURPOSE and the sim records their real size rather than holding them to the
// 200-tile floor the rest meet:
//
//   the Slayer master   37 tiles, which is Duradel's room. The point is to be put down beside him.
//   the Ectofuntus      3 tiles, a strip in the slime cavern with gloop on both sides and the
//                       cavern stairs on the tile next to it. Collision cannot follow a stair, so
//                       the flood fill stops at 3 and the player is not trapped - they are stood
//                       exactly where the buckets get filled, which is the chore the teleport is
//                       for. Note this is the SLIME PIT and not the Ectofuntus itself.

^diary_coord_ardougne_monastery = 0_40_50_46_22   // (2606,3222)  the monastery, by its own monk
^diary_coord_ardougne_farm = 0_41_52_44_46        // (2668,3374)  the farm teleport's own arrival
^diary_coord_nardah = 0_53_45_35_34               // (3427,2914)
^diary_coord_kalphite_cave = 0_50_48_27_34        // (3227,3106)  the old man's hole in the sand
^diary_coord_rellekka = 0_41_57_34_10             // (2658,3658)  inside the town, by the longhall
^diary_coord_seers_village = 0_42_54_38_32        // (2726,3488)
^diary_coord_ectofuntus = 0_57_154_35_32          // (3683,9888)  the slime cavern, at the gloop
^diary_coord_burgh_de_rott = 0_54_50_29_39        // (3485,3239)  among the villagers
^diary_coord_shilo_gem_mine = 0_44_46_10_54       // (2826,2998)  the surface gem rocks by Shilo
^diary_coord_slayer_master = 1_44_46_53_36        // (2869,2980) level 1  in the room with Duradel
^diary_coord_fountain_of_rune = 0_52_60_42_54     // (3370,3894)  deep Wilderness, deliberately

// THE WILDERNESS CEILING, 30, which is what the farm teleport uses (^farm_tele_wildy_max) and what
// dragonstone jewellery uses. It is a ceiling on where you may teleport FROM, not to - which is why
// the Wilderness sword can still drop you at the Fountain of Rune at level 36. A free escape from
// deep Wilderness is the one thing a convenience teleport must not be.
^diary_tele_wildy_max = 30

// ============================================================================ Falador shield 4
//
// TWO FULL RECHARGES A DAY, which is Old School's number for the elite shield (tiers 1-3 get one).
^falador_shield_uses_per_day = 2

// The day boundary. world_minute counts real-world minutes from 1 January 2025 00:00 UTC
// (engine/src/engine/script/ScriptOpcode.ts), so dividing by 1440 gives a day index whose
// boundaries are UTC midnight - the same reset Old School's dailies use. Minutes rather than game
// ticks is what makes the reset survive a world restart and pass while the player is logged out,
// which is also why farming's growth clock reads the same counter.
^diary_minutes_per_day = 1440

// ============================================================================ Varrock armour 4
//
// 10 PER CENT, Old School's rate, rolled per ore mined. The second ore pays its own experience, so
// the armour is a 10% boost to both ore and Mining xp at the rocks it covers.
^varrock_armour_ore_chance = 10
